---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {stylesheet} from '../../../data/assets.js';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const materials=['solid','glass','soft','veil'];
const motions=['subtle','expressive','none'];
const fills=['gradient','solid'];
const effects=[
  {id:'plain',label:'Original material',surface:false},
  {id:'material',label:'Gradient background',surface:true},
];
const sampleMarkup=(material,motion,fill,effect)=>`<section class="hero${effect.surface?' gradient-background':''}" data-material="${material}" data-motion="${motion}" data-fill="${fill}">
  <h3>Let ideas shine through.</h3>
  <p>Native content, ordinary theme text.</p>
</section>`;
---
<Layout title="Hero and animated gradients" current="hero" documentation>
  <Fragment slot="head">{['reva.hero.css','reva.gradients.css'].map(file=><link rel="stylesheet" href={stylesheet(file)}/>)}</Fragment>
  <div class="hero-showcase">
    <header><p class="doc-kicker">NATIVE CSS · SOURCE PREVIEW</p><h1>Hero and gradient effects.</h1><p>Material backgrounds animate while text uses ordinary theme colours. The letters and content remain still.</p><p><a href={base+'components/hero/'}>Hero markup</a> · <a href={base+'components/gradients/'}>Gradient effects and options</a></p></header>
    <p><a href="#gradient-state-demos">Compare original and animated materials</a></p>
    <label class="pause-control"><input id="hero-pause" type="checkbox"/> Pause gradient animations</label>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" data-material="solid" data-motion="subtle" aria-labelledby="hero-subtle-title">
      <header>
      <h2 id="hero-subtle-title">Build <span>something remarkable.</span></h2>
      <p>The primary colour sweeps between 25% darker and 25% lighter shades. Subtle motion takes 12 seconds in each direction.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#glass-hero-demo">Explore the glass hero</a>
      </header>
    </section>
    <div class="hero-backdrop" id="glass-hero-demo">
      <section class="hero gradient-background" data-material="glass" data-motion="subtle" aria-labelledby="hero-glass-title">
        <h2 id="hero-glass-title">Let your ideas <span>shine through.</span></h2>
        <p>The glass surface’s own highlight gradient moves slowly. The backdrop stays still; its transparency and blur are unchanged.</p>
        <a class="button" href="#hero-expressive-demo">Compare expressive motion</a>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" id="hero-expressive-demo" data-material="solid" data-motion="expressive" aria-labelledby="hero-expressive-title">
      <header><h2 id="hero-expressive-title">A little more <span>colour in motion.</span></h2><p>Expressive motion uses the same smooth effect over 6 seconds in each direction.</p><a class="button" href="#hero-static-demo">See the static version</a></header>
      <figure><img src={base+'images/example-landscape.svg'} width="640" height="360" alt="Illustrated hills beneath the sun"/></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" id="hero-static-demo" data-material="solid" data-motion="none" aria-labelledby="hero-static-title">
      <header>
      <h2 id="hero-static-title">Still <span>full of colour.</span></h2><p>Motion none keeps the gradient static. Reduced motion also stops the background animation automatically.</p><a class="button" href={base+'components/gradients/'}>Read the component guide</a>
      </header>
    </section>
    <section id="gradient-state-demos" aria-labelledby="gradient-state-title">
      <h2 id="gradient-state-title">Compare every material gradient state</h2>
      <p>Use Customize to switch the theme and accent for every example. Non-Glass backgrounds mix the selected primary with 25% black and 25% white; Glass keeps its existing transparent sheen. Each group compares the original material with its gradient background effect. Text has no gradient or animation.</p>
      <p>Subtle: 12 seconds per direction. Expressive: 6 seconds. None: static gradients. The pause checkbox above stops every moving example.</p>
      <p>Fill controls the material’s existing sheen. The background gradient class is independent of fill; Glass with solid fill has no sheen to move. Soft and Veil use the added surface gradient; Glass moves its own highlight.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Gradient demo materials"><ul>{materials.map(material=><li><a href={'#gradient-material-'+material}>{material}</a></li>)}</ul></nav>
      {materials.map(material=><section id={'gradient-material-'+material} class="gradient-material-group" aria-labelledby={'gradient-material-title-'+material}>
        <h3 id={'gradient-material-title-'+material}>{material.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+material.slice(1)}</h3>
        {motions.map(motion=>fills.map(fill=><details class="gradient-state-group">
          <summary>{motion.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+motion.slice(1)} motion · {fill} fill · 2 examples</summary>
          <div class="gradient-comparisons">
            {effects.map(effect=>{
              const id=`gradient-${material}-${motion}-${fill}-${effect.id}`;
              return <div class="gradient-comparison">
                <h4>{effect.label}</h4>
                <div class="hero-backdrop">
                  <section class:list={['hero','gradient-sample',{'gradient-background':effect.surface}]} data-material={material} data-motion={motion} data-fill={fill} aria-labelledby={id}>
                    <h5 id={id}>Let ideas shine through.</h5>
                    <p>Native content, ordinary theme text.</p>
                  </section>
                </div>
                <details><summary>HTML</summary><pre><code>{sampleMarkup(material,motion,fill,effect)}</code></pre></details>
              </div>;
            })}
          </div>
        </details>))}
      </section>)}
      <p>System reduced motion keeps gradients static. Higher contrast and print restore solid text and remove surface animation; reduced transparency removes surface animation. These preferences follow the device settings.</p>
    </section>
    <p>New source preview: visual/browser acceptance is pending. Check your selected colours against the actual background, especially custom photographs and translucent surfaces.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style is:global>
.hero-showcase { display:grid; gap:2rem; padding-block:2rem; }
.gradient-material-group { margin-block:2rem; scroll-margin-block-start:6rem; }
.gradient-comparisons { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,18rem),1fr)); gap:1.5rem; padding-block:1rem; }
.gradient-comparison { min-inline-size:0; }
.gradient-comparison > h4 { margin-block:0 1rem; }
.gradient-sample { padding:2rem 1.25rem; }
.gradient-sample > h5 { margin:0; font-size:clamp(1.75rem,3vw,2.5rem); line-height:1.15; overflow-wrap:anywhere; text-wrap:balance; }
.gradient-state-group { margin-block:1rem; }
.gradient-comparison pre { max-inline-size:100%; overflow:auto; }
.hero-showcase > header { max-inline-size:65ch; }
.hero-backdrop { padding:clamp(.5rem,2vw,2rem); border-radius:var(--re-radius); background:var(--re-bg); }
.hero-showcase:has(#hero-pause:checked) .gradient-background,
.hero-showcase:has(#hero-pause:checked) .gradient-background::before { animation-play-state:paused; }
@media (forced-colors:active), print { .hero-backdrop { background:transparent; } }
</style>
